abstract: "The matrix geometric mean A#B is continuous on positive definite pairs but not at singular ones. This package proves that X is a limit of A_j#B_j with positive definite A_j -> A, B_j -> B exactly when X >= 0, the block matrix [[A, X], [X, B]] is positive semidefinite and its rank is at most the dimension; gives the full set of limits at equal inputs and the exact interval of limiting Matsumoto fidelities; constructs bounded positive definite GLT matrix-sequences with identical scalar symbols whose geometric means have the wrong symbol (4/5 instead of 1 on half the interval) or no eigenvalue distribution, refuting the unrestricted symbol formula and conjecture of Ilyas, Khan, Loi and Serra-Capizzano (2025); and proves closure when the sum of the symbols is positive definite (every Kubo-Ando mean), a one-sided upper-envelope theorem, and a sharp dichotomy for bounded Riemann-integrable scalar symbols of the space variable. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text and figures CC0-1.0; code MIT."
